From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thibaut Lapierre <root@epheo.eu>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:35:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/18] ovn: enable network segmentation

UserDefinedNetwork and ClusterUserDefinedNetwork served, primary networks
included, as on OpenShift: enable-network-segmentation and
enable-preconfigured-udn-addresses in ovnkube.conf, --enable-persistent-ips
on the cluster manager (OpenShift passes it there alone), the UDN, CUDN
and IPAMClaim CRDs in MicroShift's CRD list so they exist before OVN-K
starts, and the cluster manager's rights to render NADs and own the
networks' status, and mirror each Service's EndpointSlices into the networks
that use it. Needs 0001.

With segmentation on, OVN-K isolates primary networks from the host and
lets only kubelet's cgroup through, for probes. The 5.0 OVN-K looks for a
cgroup named kubelet.service, absent here: kubelet runs inside
microshift.service, and ovnkube-node exits. ovn-kubernetes #6735 adds
kubelet-cgroup-path (OpenShift 5.1). Until the payload carries it, every
container that runs ovnkube mounts /usr/libexec/microshift-ovnkube, the
image's own ovnkube rebuilt by src/ovn/build-ovnkube.sh with #6735 and a fix
for UDN traffic to DNS and the API over a br-ex without an uplink, and
[ovnkubenode] names microshift.service. The node side also mounts
systemd's private socket, as OpenShift does, so the rule follows
microshift.service restarts. Once the payload carries both fixes the
ovnkube mounts go; the setting and the socket stay.

udn-allowed-default-services names MicroShift's DNS Service: OVN-K's
default, kube-system/kube-dns, does not exist here. dns-service-namespace
and dns-service-name give the same Service to the DHCP OVN-K serves VMs on
a primary layer2 network.

The CRD files are not carried: the SRPM stage writes them from the
payload's cluster-network-operator (src/image/payload-crds.sh). The
namespace-label admission policy and the UDN user roles come from the same
operator through src/rbac/vendor.sh.

Upstream: no config knob as of 5.0.
Covered by: vm-test (two primary CUDNs isolate their namespaces from each
other and from the default network, each still reaches DNS and the API, a
kubelet readiness probe passes into one, an IPAMClaim keeps a pod's
address across a recreate) and multinode-test (a primary CUDN spans
nodes).
